# M1_HH.xps -- runs M1_HH.ode in one go (the steps at the top of the .ode).
#   XPPAUT 8.4:  File > Do script > M1_HH.xps    (or: xppaut M1_HH.ode -script M1_HH.xps)
#   XPPAUT-Web:  pick it under Scripts (group iso-test), or open the link with ?script=
speed 0.3
msg "M1, brute force: integrate every starting point of a grid and read its phase from its spikes"

# A. window 1: the phase map, each starting point coloured by its phase theta (periodic colours)
keys v 2
ans X-axis=vs|Y-axis=ns|Xmin=-90|Ymin=0.3|Xmax=52|Ymax=0.8|Xlabel=v|Ylabel=n
keys u c a
ans theta
ans c
ans 0
ans 1
keys esc
msg "2par range over the starting point: 70 x 70 = 4900 runs, one dot each (a few minutes)"
keys i 2
ans Vary1=vs|Start1=-90|End1=52|Vary2=ns|Start2=0.3|End2=0.8|Steps=70|Steps2=70|Reset storage (Y/N)=N|Use old ic's (Y/N)=Y|Cycle color (Y/N)=N|Movie(Y/N)=N|Crv(1) Array(2)=2
keys n n
msg "Window 1: the phase map; points of one colour have the same phase, so the colour bands are the isochrons. Nullclines on top."
wait 4

# B. window 2: the same runs, only the starting points whose phase is near 0, 0.1, ..., 0.9
#    (a new window copies the colour settings but not the quantity: set it, then switch
#    colour off for this window)
keys m c
keys u c a
ans theta
ans c
ans 0
ans 1
keys esc
keys u c n
keys esc
keys v 2
ans X-axis=vb|Y-axis=nb|Xmin=-90|Ymin=0.3|Xmax=52|Ymax=0.8|Xlabel=v|Ylabel=n
keys r
keys n n
msg "Done. Window 2: ten isochrons (phase 0, 0.1, ..., 0.9) by brute force. M1's limitation: they pile up at the equilibrium x*, see M1_limitation_pileup_HH."
